    52	def resolve_store_path(file_path: Path) -> Path:
    53	    """Resolve a .vertex or .db file to the actual store .db path.
    54	
    55	    The read-side composition of the write-side resolution: the canonical
    56	    artifact, then its index. A JSONL-canonical vertex (``store "….jsonl"``)
    57	    resolves to its derived sqlite index — see ``engine.residence``.
    58	
    59	    Resolution *materializes*: ``ensure_index`` builds the index a fresh
    60	    clone (log tracked, derived ``.db`` untracked) does not have, so the read
    61	    reports the store's contents rather than an unmaterialized store. With no
    62	    log to build from, the index stays absent and the not-yet-materialized
    63	    contract below still speaks.
    64	
    65	    Deriving it from :func:`resolve_canonical_path` rather than resolving
    66	    independently keeps one answer to "which artifact does this target name":
    67	    two resolvers that can disagree is how a writer and a reader end up on
