docs/dev/structured-surface-architecture-2026-06-27.md:373:- **rides on:** engine.vertex_search (FTS5, vertex_reader.py:1319) — re-bound VERBATIM from the dead stream verb's positional query onto read --match; the Surface search() transform calls it unchanged; fetch_fold + vertex_fold key-prefix matching (_item_matches_key precedence, commands/fetch.py:274) — --kind/--key addressing and complete-key-whole detection reuse it exactly; emit's bareword key=value parser (cmd_emit parts, commands/emit.py) and the ref=A,B comma-accumulate convention — reused as the read predicate grammar (field=value) and the --key a,b,c multi-name OR, giving read/emit symmetry; fetch_tick_windows (commands/fetch.py:1068) — already materializes chained/signed/fact_cursor/cursor_kind/cursor_preview from the tick envelope; store ticks --chain is lens-only over it — S7 grew it by one net-new param (all_names) + widened since to str|None; _run_store's existing argv[0] subcommand branch (commands/store.py:503) + the existing reanchor machinery — store ticks/stats/gc/migrate ride on the store verb's branch dispatch and reanchor re-anchors the chain after curated deletes; the one _build_parser in fold.py that BOTH dispatch forms funnel through (VERBS['read'] verb-first; app._vertex_first → implicit read vertex-first) — every new flag is first-class in both forms with zero extra wiring; the Surface's Window dataclass (limited_by/query/fields/granularity from the fixed core) — every search/budget/projection records itself there, so plain and --json encoders agree on what was sliced; the lifted salience/inbound helpers (_compute_inbound_refs/_salience/_inbound_count) the core surface already moves into surface.py — --full surfaces materialized inbound/refs without recomputation, demoting --refs into the whole view; reader.summary() per-kind counts (already computed) — store stats --by-kind is mostly a lens over existing data; the existing thread status=resolved re-emit-not-delete pattern — retract generalizes it; the fold-honors-tombstone shape is the same mechanism made first-class
docs/dev/structured-surface-architecture-2026-06-27.md:381:There are not four renderers — there are TWO encoders over the one Surface, and the plain/styled/interactive "tiers" are the single visual encoder delivered through different sinks/bits. The dict-encoder `to_dict(surface)` drives `--json` + `--fields`; the Block-encoder `fold_view(surface, fidelity, width) -> Block` drives plain, styled, and (later) interactive — plain-vs-styled is a 1-bit `use_ansi` switch at print time, interactive is the same Block painted onto a Buffer in a loop. Selection splits cleanly across the three painted axes that already exist: Format+isatty pick the ENCODER and the use_ansi bit; OutputMode picks the SINK; Fidelity picks NEITHER — it shapes the Surface CONTENT that every renderer shares. The Surface is built once, identically, BEFORE the mode branch, so the deferred interactive tier plugs in at the existing `op.interactive_handler` slot with zero change to projection or encoding. Today's default is inverted by deleting one hardcoded `use_ansi=True` that actively defeats painted's own isatty auto-detect. Open-Q#3 dissolves: one structured path — `to_dict(surface)` IS `--json`, carrying the same ranked/windowed/projected rows as plain.
docs/dev/structured-surface-architecture-2026-06-27.md:426:use_ansi INVERSION lives at cli/output.py PaintedReporter.__init__ (line 104) + the construction site cli/invocation.py:38. Today `use_ansi: bool = True` is hardcoded, and PaintedReporter.print_block passes that True straight to painted's print_block — which DEFEATS painted's own correct auto-detect (`if use_ansi is None: use_ansi = stream.isatty()`, writer.py:311). Verified: a piped `sl read project --kind decision` emits raw `^[[0m^[[1m...` today. The inversion is a DELETION of an override: derive the default from isatty (PaintedReporter already calls `sys.stdout.isatty()` in _detect_width, line 112), mirroring painted detect_context's `use_ansi = not force_plain and (is_tty or mode==INTERACTIVE)`. `--plain` (views/fold.py:361) stays as the explicit DOWN-override; `--color`/`FORCE_COLOR`/`NO_COLOR` is the UP-override.
docs/dev/structured-surface-architecture-2026-06-27.md:433:- **rides on:** painted detect_context's use_ansi formula (cli/types.py:176) — reused to derive PaintedReporter.use_ansi from isatty; the inversion is deleting the override that contradicts it; painted print_block's built-in `use_ansi is None -> stream.isatty()` auto-detect (core/writer.py:311) — the inversion stops loops from overriding it with a hardcoded True; Format/parse_format + OutputMode/parse_mode (cli/types.py:459/448), already parsed in the fold view via add_cli_args (views/fold.py:129) — the encoder/sink selection reads these axes, adds none; Fidelity, already compiled (views/fold.py:433-439) and unpacked at the dispatch seam (dispatch.py:153-156) — feeds project() directly; not re-derived; Reporter Protocol + PaintedReporter/BufferReporter (cli/output.py) — the existing single painted-boundary sink: dict-encoder rides reporter.msg, Block-encoder rides reporter.print_block; no new sink class; op.interactive_handler + the dispatch.py:114 mode branch — the interactive registration point autoresearch already uses; the deferred Surface-driven tier reuses this exact slot; _dispatch_live + painted run_cli surface delivery (dispatch.py:176,233) and painted.tui.Surface (tui/store_app.py) — the Block-onto-Buffer machinery the interactive tier reuses; interactive is a sustained sink, not a new render path; call_lens (lens_resolver.py:229) — reused to invoke the render-only fold_view(surface,...)
