commit fb3806669ecbd99c9e1d0bfda25668907d6d1651
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Aug 11 12:06:03 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Aug 11 12:06:03 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): no append may stamp past an unindexed durable line
    
    A sqlite failure after the fsync rolls the transaction back, leaving the
    line durable and the offset unstamped — recoverable, because the next open
    tails it forward. But a long-lived handle never reopens: it appended the
    next line and stamped the offset past both, burying the orphan while every
    later open reported "synced". Every append now reconciles first (one meta
    read + one stat when in sync; catch_up only on disagreement).
    
    Same commit fixes offset-trust in the other direction: a negative persisted
    offset was fed to seek() and raised OSError instead of triggering the
    promised rebuild. Any offset outside 0..filesize is metadata that cannot be
    true — rebuild.
    
    Findings 1 (blocker) and 6 of the sol r1 JSONL-canonical review.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

